#. Key:	Help
#. SourceLocation:	Plugins/ToolsBox/Source/ToolsBox/Private/Tools/PhysicsPlacer/PhysicsPlacer.cpp(104)
#: Plugins/ToolsBox/Source/ToolsBox/Private/Tools/PhysicsPlacer/PhysicsPlacer.cpp(104)
msgctxt "PhysicsPlacerTool,Help"
msgid "物理摆放工具：\n  1. 进入  生成模式  后，在视口里移动光标会从光标向前检测地面，点击即在该处生成物理物体（带偏移，默认上方 2 米掉落）。Alt+点击不生成。\n  2. 生成模式支持多个网格：从内容浏览器把 StaticMesh 拖到  生成网格列表  即可加入\n  3. 或在视口里框选/点选若干物体对象，点 获取编辑器选中 加入下方列表，再 启动模拟 让它们自由掉落；停止模拟 停下并保留当前位置。\n  4. 模拟前/中/后都可  保存当前位置  记成一份带名字的摆位；不理想时用 位置回溯 返回保存时位置。\n  （物体需带网格等 PrimitiveComponent；模拟时物体会被设为可移动并开启重力）"
msgstr "Physics Placement Tool:\n  1. After entering Spawn Mode, moving the cursor in the viewport detects the ground ahead; clicking spawns a physics object there (with offset, defaults to dropping from 2 meters above). Alt+click does not spawn.\n  2. Spawn Mode supports multiple meshes: drag a StaticMesh from the Content Browser into the Spawn Mesh List to add it.\n  3. Or box/click-select several objects in the viewport, click Get Editor Selection to add them to the list below, then Start Simulation to let them fall freely; Stop Simulation stops and keeps the current position.\n  4. Before/during/after simulation you can Save Current Position to record a named pose; if unsatisfactory, use Position Rollback to return to the saved position.\n  (Objects need a mesh or other PrimitiveComponent; during simulation they are set movable and gravity is enabled)"

